"https://api.github.com/users/jay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-06-23T18:27:11Z","updated_at":"2016-06-23T18:27:11Z","body":"I compiled both as synch and the only difference I see is in `getaddrinfo`. Both call `Curl_getaddrinfo_ex` which calls `getaddrinfo`. In Windows it returns error WSAHOST_NOT_FOUND (EAI_NONAME), but in Linux it returns success and addr receives the IP. In Windows if I add `ai_flags` `AI_NUMERICHOST` then it will work.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228140674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jay","id":965580,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/965580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay","html_url":"https://github.com/jay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228188687","html_url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/893#issuecomment-228188687","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/893","id":228188687,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyODE4ODY4Nw==","user":{"login":"bagder","id":177011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzAxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder","html_url":"https://github.com/bagder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-06-23T21:25:05Z","updated_at":"2016-06-23T21:25:05Z","body":"I was triggered by [this Firefox bug](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1276144) which points to the infamous WHATWG spec that says this URL format is legitimate and should get \"canonicalized\" to the normal numerical format and then used. The procedure is important as it would change what to send in the Host: header for a request to the target server.\n\nAn interesting variation on the same style is: `curl http://0x50.0x43.6.0x32` which also works on Linux with the stock resolver because getaddrinfo thinks its fine.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228188687/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bagder","id":177011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzAxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder","html_url":"https://github.com/bagder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228211555","html_url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/893#issuecomment-228211555","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/893","id":228211555,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyODIxMTU1NQ==","user":{"login":"jay","id":965580,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/965580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay","html_url":"https://github.com/jay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-06-23T23:04:08Z","updated_at":"2016-06-23T23:04:18Z","body":"handling it early would probably be best if we want the effective url to have the x.x.x.x ip address. here is some scratch i put in parseurlandfill to get it working:\n\n``` diff\ndiff --git a/lib/url.c b/lib/url.c\nindex 3f0bde2..83cb6b9 100644\n--- a/lib/url.c\n+++ b/lib/url.c\n@@ -4390,6 +4390,45 @@ static CURLcode parseurlandfillconn(struct SessionHandle\n       }\n     }\n   }\n+  else {\n+    char *p;\n+    bool isneg = false;\n+    bool isintstr = true;\n+    unsigned ip = 0;\n+    for(p = conn->host.name; *p; ++p) {\n+      unsigned n;\n+      unsigned max = isneg ? (unsigned)INT_MIN : UINT_MAX;\n+      if(p == conn->host.name && *p == '-') {\n+        isneg = true;\n+        continue;\n+      }\n+      if(p - conn->host.name > 10 || *p < '0' || *p > '9') {\n+        isintstr = false;\n+        break;\n+      }\n+      n = *p - 48;\n+      if(ip > max / 10 || (ip == max / 10 && n > max % 10)) {\n+        isintstr = false;\n+        break;\n+      }\n+      ip *= 10;\n+      ip += n;\n+    }\n+    if(isintstr) {\n+      int x[4];\n+      if(isneg)\n+        ip = (unsigned)-(int)ip;\n+      x[3] = ip % 256;\n+      ip /= 256;\n+      x[2] = ip % 256;\n+      ip /= 256;\n+      x[1] = ip % 256;\n+      ip /= 256;\n+      x[0] = ip % 256;\n+      ip /= 256;\n+      snprintf(conn->host.name, 16, \"%d.%d.%d.%d\", x[0], x[1], x[2], x[3]);\n+    }\n+  }\n\n   if(data->set.scope_id)\n     /* Override any scope that was set above.  */\n```\n\nissues:\ni didn't test negative\nipv4 as ipv6\ndidn't rebuild url so that effective url shows ip\ndoesn't handle 0x50.0x43.6.0x32 shenanigans\nprobably other things\n\n```\n> GET / HTTP/1.1\n> Host: 80.67.6.50\n> User-Agent: curl/7.50.0-DEV\n> Accept: */*\n```\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228211555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jay","id":965580,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/965580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay","html_url":"https://github.com/jay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228484422","html_url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/893#issuecomment-228484422","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/893","id":228484422,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyODQ4NDQyMg==","user":{"login":"bagder","id":177011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzAxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder","html_url":"https://github.com/bagder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-06-24T23:04:24Z","updated_at":"2016-06-24T23:04:24Z","body":"> i didn't test negative\n\nI don't think negative works anywhere.\n\n> doesn't handle 0x50.0x43.6.0x32\n\nI think that's just as well!\n\n> snprintf(conn->host.name, 16, \"%\n\nCan we be certain that the target buffer is always allocated that big already? For a command line like`curl 9` for example... (which admittedly is a funny IP address, but still...)\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228484422/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bagder","id":177011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzAxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder","html_url":"https://github.com/bagder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228518663","html_url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/893#issuecomment-228518663","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/893","id":228518663,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyODUxODY2Mw==","user":{"login":"jay","id":965580,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/965580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay","html_url":"https://github.com/jay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-06-25T07:17:35Z","updated_at":"2016-09-12T20:08:48Z","body":"yes, I'm sure you're right so how about this:\n\n``` diff\ndiff --git a/lib/url.c b/lib/url.c\nindex 3f0bde2..f789aaf 100644\n--- a/lib/url.c\n+++ b/lib/url.c\n@@ -4390,6 +4390,27 @@ static CURLcode parseurlandfillconn(struct SessionHandle\n       }\n     }\n   }\n+  /* If we have an address like 1346569778 convert that to IPv4 x.x.x.x */\n+  else {\n+    char *p;\n+    unsigned ip = 0;\n+    for(p = conn->host.name; *p; ++p) {\n+      unsigned n = *p - 48;\n+      const unsigned max = 4294967295u;\n+      if(*p < '0' || *p > '9' || ip > max / 10 ||\n+         (ip == max / 10 && n > max % 10))\n+        break;\n+      ip = (ip * 10) + n;\n+    }\n+    if(p != conn->host.name && !*p) {\n+      free(conn->host.name);\n+      conn->host.name = aprintf(\"%d.%d.%d.%d\", ip / 16777216,\n+                                (ip / 65536) % 256, (ip / 256) % 256,\n+                                ip % 256);\n+      if(!conn->host.name)\n+        return CURLE_OUT_OF_MEMORY;\n+    }\n+  }\n\n   if(data->set.scope_id)\n     /* Override any scope that was set above.  */\n```\n\nissues:\nstrtol may be cleaner with some check\nhost.name iirc is actually alloc'd somewhere else so I don't think I can just free(conn->host.name) without leaving something dangling\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228518663/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jay","id":965580,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/965580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay","html_url":"https://github.com/jay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228689267","html_url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/893#issuecomment-228689267","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/893","id":228689267,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyODY4OTI2Nw==","user":{"login":"bagder","id":177011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzAxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder","html_url":"https://github.com/bagder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-06-27T08:55:58Z","updated_at":"2016-06-27T08:55:58Z","body":"> strtol may be cleaner with some check\n\nMaybe, but then again long is 64 bit on many platforms these days and I think we should leave any number using more than 32bits alone and pass it to the name resolver. So it would need some additional funny checks that may very well not make using strtol() worth it...\n\n> host.name iirc is actually alloc'd somewhere else\n\nYeah. the allocation is held in 'rawalloc'. See [this logic](https://github.com/curl/curl/blob/master/lib/url.c#L5820)\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228689267/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bagder","id":177011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzAxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder","html_url":"https://github.com/bagder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228716630","html_url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/893#issuecomment-228716630","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/893","id":228716630,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyODcxNjYzMA==","user":{"login":"bagder","id":177011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzAxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder","html_url":"https://github.com/bagder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-06-27T11:07:00Z","updated_at":"2016-06-27T11:07:00Z","body":"I'm trying to parse [that section of the WHATWG spec](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-ipv4-parser), and if I understand it correctly it seems to imply that also \"1234.1234\" should be considered a valid IPv4 address. That spec is horribly hard to read and parse at a glance, but step 14 and 15 does not limit the math to just one numerical part but can in fact be one, two or three. Perhaps. At the same time step 8 and 9 seem to contradict that so I am certainly not sure!\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228716630/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bagder","id":177011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzAxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder","html_url":"https://github.com/bagder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228943817","html_url":"https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/893#issuecomment-228943817","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/893","id":228943817,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyODk0MzgxNw==","user":{"login":"jay","id":965580,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/965580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay","html_url":"https://github.com/jay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-06-28T04:14:10Z","updated_at":"2016-06-28T04:14:10Z","body":"**IPV4 parser** 6.2 says _n is the result of parsing_. And number algorithm parsing is in **IPv4 number parser** section (it's immediately above current). In **IPv4 number parser** the last step of the number parser is _\"Return the mathematical integer value that is represented by input in radix-R notation\"_. So if you have 65535 you return that. Then back at step 8 of **IPV4 parser** it says _\"If any item in numbers is greater than 255, syntax violation\"_.\n\nIn any case what I wrote isn't compatible with all that since it only does base 10 with no separators.  Also the effective url should maybe be changed, probably by parsing earlier and repairing the url in that case.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/comments/228943817/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jay","id":965580,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTU4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/965580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay","html_url":"https://github.com/jay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/user